DXMT port snapshot
==================

Repository: https://github.com/3Shain/dxmt.git
Base: 589adb780354b461645b29999cefaf533594ee99 (v0.80) with 0001 and 0002 from
this directory applied and committed as "Kitsune base". That commit is the
pre-image of ios-dxmt-full-vs-upstream.patch.

  0001-xcode27-metal-and-libcxx-fixes.patch  builds v0.80 with Xcode 27's Metal
                                             compiler, current libc++ and
                                             Homebrew's llvm@15
  0002-winemetal-ios-unix-half.patch         winemetal's unix half for iOS:
                                             macOS-only APIs guarded, iOS AIR
                                             triple, sandbox-safe Metal cache
                                             path
  ios-dxmt-full-vs-upstream.patch            the rest of the port, over the
                                             base commit

scripts/apply-dxmt-port.sh creates the base commit and applies the full patch.
scripts/10-dxmt.sh builds the PE half, scripts/15-dxmt-ios.sh the iOS unix
half (winemetal.so). scripts/save-patches.sh regenerates the full patch from
the working tree.

d3d11.dll and winemetal.so change together: the shader cache ABI and the
constant-buffer argument layout are shared. Ship both or neither.

Contents beyond upstream: iOS support in winemetal, Managed-to-Shared storage
on iOS, CPU BC1..BC7 decode (bcdec, MIT, src/dxmt/bcdec.h) with an optional
16-bit BC1 path behind KITSUNE_BC_16BIT=1, BC mip capping with logical
descriptors, ETC2/EAC transcode (etcpak, BSD-3, src/winemetal/unix/etcpak)
behind KITSUNE_BC_NATIVE=1, constant-buffer bounds checks, GPU debug mask
(Documents/dxmt-gpu-debug.txt), nil drawable handling (testable with
KITSUNE_NIL_DRAWABLE_EVERY=N), and present count, GPU busy time and frame cap
hooks for the app.
